	"sources": [
		"ESP32-WROOM-32E & WROOM-32UE datasheet v2.1, Table 3 pin definitions (38 pads; GPIO6–11 go to the module's SPI flash and are not led out, pads 17–22 NC; GPIO34–39 input only; IO16 taken by PSRAM on the -N4R2/-N8R2 variants, free on -N4), pad 39 the ground pad (§11.1, soldering it optional)",
		"ESP32 Series datasheet v5.3: strapping pins GPIO0, GPIO2, MTDI (GPIO12: sets the flash voltage, must be low at reset on a 3.3 V-flash module), MTDO (GPIO15), GPIO5; RTC GPIOs (deep-sleep wake) 0, 2, 4, 12–15, 25–27, 32–39; ADC2 is unusable while Wi-Fi runs, so only ADC1 channels are listed",
		"Espressif's own ESP32 boards flash over UART0 (GPIO1/GPIO3) through a USB-UART bridge, GPIO0 low at reset selects download boot"
	]
